  "title": "School Funds Day.",
  "body": " School Funds Day   For a school funds day, the student council buys crates of soda at Ksh each, which make a profit of Ksh each, and cartons of juice at Ksh each, which make a profit of Ksh each. It has Ksh to spend and space in the store for crates and cartons. What should it buy?    Let be the number of crates of soda and the number of cartons of juice. Money: , that is . Space: . Also , , whole numbers. Maximise .  The sloping boundaries meet where , so : . The vertices are , , and , with , , and .  The best vertex is not a whole-number point. costs Ksh , more than the money available. Near the vertex: , , , .  The council should buy crates of soda and cartons of juice, for a profit of Ksh . Check: shillings and items.  Check with a search line: the gradient of is , between (space) and (money), so is the best vertex, and is the first whole-number point of R the line meets as it slides back.   "
