  "body": " Inverse Transformations       Strand  2.0 Measurements and Geometry    Sub-Strand  2.1 Matrices and Transformations    Specific Learning Outcomes  Determine an inverse of a transformation in different situations          Back to the Start   A triangle was transformed by the matrix . Its image has vertices , and . Nobody wrote down the original triangle.     Find , using the Grade 11 formula.    Write the image vertices as the columns of a matrix and multiply it by .    Check your answer: apply to your three points.    Work out . Why does this mean that  undoes  ?        The Inverse Transformation  The inverse transformation of a transformation with matrix sends every image point back onto its object. Its matrix is the inverse matrix The inverse undoes the transformation, so it sends every image point back to where it came from. If there is no inverse matrix and no inverse transformation ( shows why).  Inverses of the standard transformations: a reflection is its own inverse; a rotation through anticlockwise about is undone by a rotation through clockwise; the enlargement, centre , scale factor is undone by the enlargement, centre , scale factor .  To undo two transformations, undo the last one first. If is followed by , the single matrix is , and the transformation that undoes both is followed by :     Press the button: the inverse matrix moves the image back onto the object.     Finding the Object   The matrix maps onto and onto . Find and .    Step 1: the inverse.  , so   Step 2: apply it to the images.  So and .  Step 3: check.  , which is .     Inverses of Standard Transformations   State the inverse of each transformation in words, and check it by multiplying the matrices.  The rotation of anticlockwise about .  The reflection in the -axis.  The enlargement, centre , scale factor .      (a) The inverse is the rotation of clockwise about :   (b) The reflection is its own inverse: reflecting twice in the same line brings every point back.   (c) The inverse is the enlargement, centre , scale factor : Each product is the identity , so the two matrices in each pair undo each other.     Undoing Two Transformations   A point is transformed by , and its image is then reflected in the line (matrix ). The final image is . Find the matrix that undoes both transformations, and the original point.    Method 1: invert the single matrix.  is done first, so the single matrix is Its determinant is , so .  Method 2: undo the last one first.  is its own inverse, and . Undo first, then : the same matrix.  The original point is . Check: .    Type one number in each box of a matrix. Type fractions with a slash, for example -3\/2 , or as decimals, for example -1.5 . Type each coordinate in its own box.             . Find , and the object whose image under is .  ;    Describe fully the inverse of each transformation.  The rotation of clockwise about .  The reflection in the line .  The enlargement, centre , scale factor .    (a) the rotation of anticlockwise about (b) the reflection in the line itself (c) the enlargement, centre , scale factor    . Find the images of , and . Explain why has no inverse transformation.  , , , all on the line ; , so there is no inverse.  Each image has , and so does the image of every point, because and . Many different points have the same image (for example and both go to ), so from an image there is no way to tell which point it came from. Also , so does not exist.    A point is rotated anticlockwise about and then enlarged, centre , scale factor . Its final image is . Find the matrix that undoes both transformations, and the original point.  ;  Undo the last one first: the enlargement by , then the rotation of clockwise. The matrix is , and it sends to .    A faulty printer at a cyber café in Kisumu distorts every design by the matrix . Two corners of a printed design are at and . Where were these corners in the original design?  and  The determinant is , so the inverse is . Then .    Challenge: A Matrix That Undoes Itself  Show that is its own inverse. What happens to a point that is transformed by this matrix twice?  Work out the square of the matrix.  Its square is ; the point returns to where it started.  . So the matrix times itself is , which means it is its own inverse: the second transformation undoes the first and the point returns to its start.    "
