  "title": "Area Scale Factor and Determinant of a Matrix",
  "body": " Area Scale Factor and Determinant of a Matrix       Strand  2.0 Measurements and Geometry    Sub-Strand  2.1 Matrices and Transformations    Specific Learning Outcomes  Relate area scale factor to determinant of a matrix in different situations          How Much Bigger?   The rectangle has vertices , , and , lettered anticlockwise. Its area is square units. Four matrices are      Draw the image of under each matrix and find its area.    Find the determinant of each matrix.    For each matrix, work out (area of image) (area of object). Compare it with the determinant.    Letter each image . Which image is lettered clockwise?    What happened to the rectangle under ?        Area Scale Factor  For a transformation with matrix , every area is multiplied by the same number, the area scale factor , which is the size of the determinant:   The sign of tells you about the orientation of the image. If , vertices lettered anticlockwise in the object are still anticlockwise in the image. If , the orientation is reversed: anticlockwise lettering becomes clockwise, and the shape has been turned over (the transformation includes a reflection). If , the image of every shape lies on a line through ; its area is and has no inverse.  The determinant tells you how many times bigger every area becomes, and its sign tells you whether the shape has been turned over. For two successive transformations the area scale factors multiply: .    The unit square has area . Its image under is a parallelogram of area , the determinant of the matrix.   The unit square O(0, 0), A(1, 0), B(1, 1), C(0, 1), shaded, and its image, the parallelogram O, A prime(2, 1), B prime(3, 5), C prime(1, 4), drawn dashed. The square has area 1 and the parallelogram has area 7.      Change the matrix. The area of the image always equals the size of the determinant.     Area of an Image   The triangle with , and is mapped by . Find the area of the image and describe its orientation.    The triangle has a right angle at , with sides and , so its area is square units.  . The area scale factor is , so the image has area square units.  The determinant is negative, so the orientation is reversed. Check with the images:  runs anticlockwise, but , , runs clockwise ( ).     The triangle is lettered anticlockwise; its image under is lettered clockwise.   Triangle A(1, 1), B(5, 1), C(1, 4), with a curved arrow showing that A, B, C runs anticlockwise. Its image, drawn dashed, A prime(4, 0), B prime(24, 4), C prime(1, -3), with a curved arrow showing that A prime, B prime, C prime runs clockwise.      Finding an Unknown Entry   The matrix maps a shape of area square units onto a shape of area square units. Find the two possible values of .    The area scale factor is , so . Here , so giving or . With the orientation is kept; with (determinant ) it is reversed.     When the Image Collapses   Find the value of for which has no inverse. For this value, show that the image of every point lies on one line, and find the line.    There is no inverse when the determinant is : , so .  Then The first coordinate of every image is twice the second, so every image lies on the line (that is, ). For example , and go to , and ( ). Every shape is flattened onto this line, so its image has area , and many points share one image, so the transformation cannot be undone.     Under the whole plane collapses onto the line .   The unit square O, A(1, 0), B(1, 1), C(0, 1) and the line x = 2y through O. Under the matrix with rows 4, 6 and 2, 3 the points A, C and B go to A prime(4, 2), C prime(6, 3) and B prime(10, 5), all on the line.     Type one number in each box of a matrix. Type fractions with a slash, for example -3\/2 , or as exact decimals, for example -1.5 .             A square of area square units is mapped by each matrix below. For each, find the determinant, the area of the image, and whether the orientation is kept or reversed.      (a) ; square units; kept (b) ; square units; reversed    The triangle with vertices , and is mapped by . Find the area of the image.  square units  The triangle has area . The determinant is , so the image has area square units.    Find the value of for which has no inverse. For this value, find the line onto which the whole plane collapses.  ; the line  gives . Then , and the second coordinate is always twice the first, so every image lies on .    The matrix maps a shape of area square units onto a shape of area square units. Find both possible values of .  or  The area scale factor is . The determinant is , so or , giving or .    A rectangular shamba near Nakuru measures by . A farmer draws it on a plan, using the matrix to change the real measurements into plan units. What is the area of the shamba on the plan, in square plan units?  square plan units  The real area is . The determinant is , so the area on the plan is square plan units. (Check: the plan rectangle is by .)    Challenge: The Determinant of a Product  and . Show that , and explain this result using area scale factors.  is the single matrix for two transformations. Each one has its own area scale factor.  ,  , so . Also and , and . means followed by : multiplies every area by , and then multiplies every area by , so together every area is multiplied by .    "
