  "title": "Challenge: Round a Triangle.",
  "body": " Challenge: Round a Triangle  Find the length of the locus of points outside an equilateral triangle of side that are from the nearest side or corner of the triangle. Give your answer correct to 1 decimal place.  What does the locus look like near each corner, and what do the three corner arcs add up to?   Along each side the locus is a segment of , parallel to the side and outside it. At each corner the nearest point of the triangle is the corner itself, so the locus is an arc of radius centred at the corner. Each arc turns through , and the three arcs together make a whole circle. The length is .  "
