  "body": " Regions from Loci  A condition with less than or more than gives a region , not a line or curve. The locus of the matching equals condition is its boundary .    : inside the circle with centre and radius ; : outside it.  : the side of the perpendicular bisector of that contains .  Distance from a line less than : the strip between the two lines parallel to at distance .  Angle , on one side of : inside the arc of the constant angle locus, between the arc and ; angle : outside the arc.    Draw a boundary solid when it belongs to the region ( , ) and dashed when it does not ( , ). For each condition, shade the side of its boundary that is not wanted. The region left clear obeys every condition, and a key says so: shaded, not wanted; unshaded, the required region ( ).  "
