  "body": " Coordinates in Three Dimensions  Three axes , and meet at the origin , each at right angles to the other two. Think of the - and -axes on the floor and the -axis going up a corner of the room. The coordinates of a point tell you how far along each of the three axes you must move from to reach .  The three coordinate planes are the -plane (where ), the -plane ( ) and the -plane ( ). Points on the axes have two zero coordinates: , and .  The moves from to form the column and the midpoint of is , just as in two dimensions.  "
