  "id": "ex-ships-clock",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "sec-longitude-and-time.html#ex-ships-clock",
  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "11.4.2.4",
  "title": "Challenge: The Ship’s Clock.",
  "body": " Challenge: The Ship's Clock  A ship sails due west along the equator, covering each day. Its clock is set to local time once a day. By how much is the clock changed each day, and is it put forward or back?  How many degrees of longitude is along the equator?  Back minutes each day  a day. minutes. The ship moves west, where local time is behind, so the clock is put back minutes each day.  "
