  "url": "sec-quartiles-deciles-and-percentiles-for-grouped-data.html#insight-reading-the-curve",
  "type": "Key Takeaway",
  "number": "12.3.22",
  "title": "Reading the Curve.",
  "body": " Reading the Curve  To estimate a median or quartile from a cumulative frequency curve, find its position ( , or ) on the cumulative frequency axis, go across to the curve, then down to the horizontal axis.  The interquartile range is , the spread of the middle half of the data. The quartile deviation (or semi-interquartile range) is half of it, .  Deciles and percentiles are read in the same way, going across from or .  "
